WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.930
Look, I don't see what the big deal is.

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.010
So as you might've heard a
lawyer appeared in court as a cat

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:06.843
Let's watch:

00:00:06.843 --> 00:00:09.330
- Pardon? I believe you
have a filter turned

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.860
on in the video settings.
- Yeah, you think?

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:12.693
I think that's a filter.

00:00:12.693 --> 00:00:14.451
- You might want to, uh,

00:00:14.451 --> 00:00:15.444
take a look.

00:00:15.444 --> 00:00:17.130
- Uh, we're trying to--

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.190
Can you hear me, judge?

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.432
- I can hear you. I think it's a filter.

00:00:20.432 --> 00:00:24.090
- If it is, I don't know how to remove it.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.300
- God, we've all been there

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.350
with technical difficulties
that you can't fix.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.050
- I'm prepared to go forward with it.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.340
That's-- I'm here live. I'm not a cat.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.817
- Ha ha! That's gotta be one for the ages.

00:00:34.817 --> 00:00:36.250
"I'm here live. I'm not a cat."

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.660
Look. The overall lesson here is that

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.180
things go wrong in court all the time

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.320
and the judge says that this
lawyer handled it with grace

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.910
and composure and you just
gotta roll with the punches.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.370
Especially in this pandemic world,

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.610
you've got to deal with
things like video conferencing

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.030
but the other lesson is
if you're going to have

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.442
a video conference with the judge

00:00:50.442 --> 00:00:52.410
make sure that A: you're wearing pants

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.087
and B: you're not a cat

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.590
#NotLegalAdvice

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.340
but this is advice: subscribe
or I'll see you in court.

